{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0114aAdRR7hpLw5CmNc3kBJL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs. This project extracts specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go binaries), `pkg/sys/` (platform syscall abstraction), `pkg/format/` (shared output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets).\n\n**Current state**: `pkg/sys/` and `pkg/format/` have source code on the working branch (confirmed in source_code). `pkg/testutils/` has no source code on the working branch. Specs are complete for all rel00.0 use cases.\n\n**Release 00.0 use cases**:\n- uc001-magefiles — excluded by DD7 (magefiles/ path; cmd/version is the only code target but depends on other infrastructure)\n- uc002-format — **done** (source code exists: color.go, column.go, size.go)\n- uc003-sys — **done** (source code exists: fileinfo.go, fileinfo_darwin.go, fileinfo_linux.go, terminal.go)\n- uc004-testutils — **not started** (no source code on working branch)\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe only remaining rel00.0 code target with no source code is `pkg/testutils/`. It is foundational infrastructure — every `cmd/` utility's differential tests depend on it. Per P5 (libraries before consumers) and P8 (libraries before CLI), this must be built before any `cmd/` utility tests.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/testutils: DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests execution harness\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - \"docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find the testutils PRD -- expected name prd004-testutils.yaml or prd*-testutils*.yaml)\"\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils component section)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml (testutils use case)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (existing pkg/ code style and patterns)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (existing pkg/ code style -- copyright header, doc comments, Implements tags)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests harness function\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Define DiffTest as the primary exported struct for the package. Include\n          fields for the Go binary path, the reference binary path, input\n          arguments ([]string), stdin content, environment variables ([]string),\n          expected exit code, and a test name or description. Match exact field\n          names and types from the testutils PRD.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement RunDiffTests accepting *testing.T and a slice of DiffTest.\n          For each test case, execute both the Go binary and the reference binary\n          using os/exec with identical arguments, stdin, and environment. Capture\n          stdout, stderr, and exit code from both executions.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Compare stdout, stderr, and exit code between the two binary runs.\n          Report divergences using t.Errorf with the test name, the input that\n          triggered the divergence, expected output (reference binary), and\n          actual output (Go binary).\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Support optional normalization functions per DiffTest that transform\n          stdout and stderr before comparison. When no normalizer is configured,\n          comparison is byte-for-byte exact. This handles known acceptable\n          differences such as timestamp formatting or binary name references in\n          error messages.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Primary file is difftest.go, named after the DiffTest type per project\n          convention (see P7 in project rules -- the primary source file is named\n          after the primary exported type, not the package name).\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Follow existing pkg/ code style: copyright header \"Copyright (c) 2026\n          Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\", SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT,\n          package-level doc comment referencing the PRD, and per-function\n          \"Implements: prdNNN RX.Y\" comments on exported symbols. See\n          pkg/sys/fileinfo.go and pkg/format/size.go for reference.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: pkg/testutils/difftest.go compiles with \"go build ./pkg/testutils/\".\n      - id: AC2\n        text: |\n          DiffTest struct is exported with fields for binary paths, arguments,\n          stdin, environment, expected exit code, test name, and optional\n          normalization function.\n      - id: AC3\n        text: |\n          RunDiffTests is exported, accepts *testing.T and []DiffTest, executes\n          both binaries per test case, and reports divergences via t.Errorf.\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/\" reports no errors.\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21658,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21658},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a444cf88-de46-4fa6-8504-e03f1b25a933","uuid":"4fa680d0-be6f-45e2-b638-70cd80a4cf3c"}
